{"id": "en_avalanche_p2", "total": 69.97, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. Heavy snow traps Jake with an air pocket while his partner lacks a shovel.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.06}, {"text": "The packed white debris locks his limbs completely while the 15 minute clock ticks down.", "start": 4.54, "end": 8.3}, {"text": "His climbing partner turns on a rescue beacon to locate Jake under the dense snow.", "start": 8.86, "end": 12.32}, {"text": "A nearby backcountry skier hears the emergency signal and rushes over with full safety gear.", "start": 12.92, "end": 16.88}, {"text": "One. Always carry proper avalanche safety gear like a working beacon, probe, and shovel.", "start": 17.264, "end": 21.42}, {"text": "The arriving rescuer uses a metal probe to pinpoint Jake beneath the heavy snow layer.", "start": 21.94, "end": 25.48}, {"text": "Two. Move fast because most buried victims must be dug out within about 15 minutes.", "start": 25.946, "end": 30.28}, {"text": "The rescuer starts digging furiously with a sturdy shovel to clear the packed snow.", "start": 30.8, "end": 33.9}, {"text": "Jake stays calm inside his air pocket while snow squeezes hard against his tight chest.", "start": 34.54, "end": 38.14}, {"text": "Three. Cup one arm in front of your face to protect your airway under debris.", "start": 38.57, "end": 42.1}, {"text": "The shovel breaks through the top layer right above Jake's raised waving bare hand.", "start": 42.64, "end": 46.2}, {"text": "Fresh cold air enters the tiny pocket as rescuers clear snow off his face fast.", "start": 46.74, "end": 50.38}, {"text": "They pull Jake out from beneath the rock overhang before his emergency air runs out.", "start": 50.96, "end": 54.14}, {"text": "Rescue gear like a beacon, probe, and shovel saved his life on this cold peak.", "start": 54.7, "end": 58.2}, {"text": "Never enter avalanche territory without the essential 3 rescue tools for emergency fast survival.", "start": 58.74, "end": 62.96}, {"text": "Always carry es